 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "pesachim.65a.2",
   "daf": "65a",
   "sentenceId": 1,
   "he": "יָצְתָה כַּת רִאשׁוֹנָה וְכוּ׳. תָּנָא: הִיא נִקְרֵאת כַּת עַצְלָנִית. וְהָא לָא סַגִּי דְּלָאו הָכִי, מַאי הָוֵי לְהוּ לְמִיעְבַּד?",
   "en": "It was stated in the next clause of the mishna that after «the first group exited,» the second group and then the third group would enter. «It was taught» in the Tosefta with regard to the third group: «It was called the lazy group» because it was the last of the three groups. The Gemara asks: «But it would not have been sufficient without this» third group, as the Paschal lamb must be offered in three shifts. «What,» then, «should» the members of the third group «have done?»"
  }
 ],
